						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=2063">Aamain</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/25/2002 - 11:28 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=1578">Aamain Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=1962">Aamaorn Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2012">Aatun Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2034">Alladric Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2715">Aagein Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3775">Sshaamy</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2855">Coffer</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3768">Aaliam</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=1989">Aadain</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2755">Aagain</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3189">Aaralron</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2757">Aaclef</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2758">Aamaine</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2759">Rubal</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2013">Vnayil</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3039">Aakitt</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														one of the things I noted about the raid was the lack of communication that was happening between the Raid officer and the Raid Attendees...<br />
<br />
I realize that this was both an Informal raid and was our first one...with that kept in mind...<br />
<br />
with communication two things need to have happen<br />
<br />
1. we need facilitators<br />
2. People able to listen to the facilitators<br />
<br />
when everyone is talking and doing other things...that isn't condusive to a good Raid enviroment<br />
<br />
I will be posting raid guide lines of what is expected and tips on help everyone to be on the same page						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3291">Cuedyen</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/25/2002 - 12:15 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2645">Cuedyen Abuhannah</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2878">Legween Abuhannah</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Have to concur with Aamain.<br />
<br />
It was frustrating.  Before people criticize too much - they need to realize this was in informal raid.<br />
<br />
Informal pickup raids are the most frustrating because:<br />
<br />
A.  No clear goal<br />
B.  No pre-planning can be accomplished<br />
C.  People have not raided together<br />
<br />
Saying that, I am glad that everyone showed up and hopefully will show up again.<br />
<br />
One of the main problems I heard with DF was that there were no lower level raids.  Looking at this raid I can see why they were unwilling.  However - to make sure we can function effectively at higher levels we must have these lower raids.<br />
<br />
Last comments:<br />
<br />
1. Come with the intention of participating - I was annoyed to see people with their own agenda's.  Raids are guild events and we all need to support the raid officers.<br />
<br />
2.  LISTEN - aye communication problems were happening in both directions, but a lot of people (to include us higher supporting members) were not paying attention.  I was guilty as much as anyone.<br />
<br />
3.  Have fun - don't let frustration ruin your day.  In the end this is just a game.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3760">Jalanon</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/25/2002 - 1:24 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3135">Jalanon Ymus</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3152">Wenlawen Silverbow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3159">Cadilu Cadalilly</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3136">Vekaz</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3363">Grimlee</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3361">Hareey</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3362">Nasferatuu</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I for one think the raid went rather well.  Although we ended up with only 10 people in the end, we got all the way to the bottom of runnyeye and were able to kill anything and everything thrown at us, even the Lord.<br />
<br />
In addition, we got a BUNCH of good armor for melee classes.  Too bad none of our melee classes really needed it, but if the raid had been somewhere we could have gotten armor for everyone, it would have been great.<br />
<br />
Only complaints I had (in the beginning) were 1.) uneven groups.  Of course, that's to be expected when starting out.  I've hosted a number of low-mid level raids, and have noticed that the group format must be WAY different from the 40+ raids.  Just my own experience.  2.)  people need to be patient and wait for the order to go.  We had people dying in runnyeye before they were even given the order to go inside.  Raids, as I've found through experience, are not just something you can rush into expecting to kill kill kill.  In order to stay alive, you have to plan well, wait for orders, and follow them.  I agree that you can ask questions, but I swear if I heard &quot;when are we going&quot; one more time I was gonna kill someone.<br />
<br />
Bottom line, stay quiet and listen to the organizer's orders, and realize that there are stragglers who just logged on at 1:15pm when the raid was scheduled at 1pm, and we have to include them, too.  Sometimes people just can't help it.  I heard a few people say &quot;I can't stand just sitting here.&quot;  You have 2 options:  get used to it or never raid.  As you grow in this game, you'll see that raids take time.  Take Vox for instance.  I've seen countless Vox raids go wrong because everyone's in such a hurry that one person &quot;accidentally&quot; goes after her and kills all 60 people.<br />
<br />
Anyway, enough rambling on.  I think that the raid ended up going very well, and I would definately consider what we accomplished there a success.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=2967">Salorn</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/26/2002 - 1:32 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2352">Salorn Peacebringer</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I would have to agree to the posts above.<br />
<br />
What u have to realise also the zone we where raiding is a low end zone. We had people level 14-51 at the raid, so not easy to group people.<br />
<br />
I hope that no one lost any exp on this raid i did my best to res people when they died.<br />
<br />
I also admit that it was a learning curve for me.<br />
<br />
Yes i know alot of zones but i used to for my small part in last guild not DF, do the low level raids 15-35 was the norm and alot more planning would go into these as i knew well in advance what was wanted and req by all attendes.<br />
<br />
As a 1st OoN raid goes i think it went ok these things like most in game need practise.<br />
<br />
With regard to waiting around doing nothing well, Jal u are correct people will neeed to get used to it ive waited 3hrs for a Corspe retrival before and waited hours for vox naggy raids not to mention plan raids.<br />
<br />
On most big raids u have lots of group officers and all fight togeather for one purpose.<br />
<br />
Next time mybe we should do this, only prob is not all the groups get exp, ive gone on lots of raids got no loot no exp and died a few times, but thats the game.<br />
<br />
If you really want to raid then please remember the above point.<br />
<br />
Next time lets mybe try for a certain item say part of a epic that way we all know what the game plan is.<br />
<br />
Thxs<br />
SAl						</td>
					</tr>
